  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nMid level shortwave passes well to our north thru the northern Great\nLakes with a strong ridge building into the area today. This ridge\nwill continue to impact our weather into this weekend. Given the \nanomalous heights in the ridge, temperatures will continue to trend \nwell above normal values today through Sunday under a southerly flow \nregime. Given the dry air mass, overnight lows will drop into the \nmiddle 30s into the middle 40s through Saturday night, resulting in a\n25-30+ degree swing in diurnal temperatures. Expect high temperatures\nin the mid and upper 60s today thru Sunday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\n\nThe mid level ridge shifts east during the latter half of the \nweekend, as an amplified trough moves into the region. A cold front \nwill swing through the Ohio Valley Sunday night, which will usher in \nsome rain late Sunday into Sunday night. The system is progressive\nand QPF values generally remain low, with most of the area likely \nobserving less than a quarter of an inch. \n\nIn the wake of the front, a cooler air mass to remain in place at \nleast into the Thanksgiving holiday. High temperatures will generally\nbe drop back in the 40s next week. Renewed chances for precipitation\nare possible Wednesday into Thursday. With the cooler thermal \nprofiles, cannot rule out the possibility for some snowflakes to mix \nin with the rain.",
